{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","id":"msg_vrtx_01SranZhpHmWvdmP1uENt3cG","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Done. I wrote **Q29: Bad chunking (fixed-size vs semantic)** (`answers/02-029-bad-chunking-fixed-size-vs-semantic.md`).\n\nThe note covers:\n\n- **Framing** — probes whether you can diagnose chunking as the upstream root cause of retrieval failure before any model runs\n- **Answer** — four-strategy taxonomy with a failure-mode table:\n  - *Fixed-size*: splits tables mid-row, cuts code blocks, orphans cross-paragraph context\n  - *Recursive character*: LangChain default, better but still structure-blind\n  - *Semantic/structure-aware*: respects headers, code fences, HTML tags\n  - *Parent-child*: 256-token child for precise retrieval, 1024-token parent returned to LLM\n- **Benchmark methodology** — golden set Recall@5/MRR validation; real example 61%→74% on 200K-article KB\n- **Pitfalls** — \"I just used 512 because that's the default\" / \"just add more overlap\" / fixed-size on tables without naming the failure\n- **Cross-links** — Q13 (failure modes taxonomy), Q6 (PDF cross-page context), Q21 (eval methodology)\n\n5 items remain in the **Next** queue: Q30–Q34 + validate."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":352,"cache_read_input_tokens":66060,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":352,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e34af413-c6bd-4f65-b191-686de090d275","uuid":"648738d6-30a5-48db-9917-cc37f0deb300"}
